KG42.register("source_edge_archive-0ac2796dc2a0d39ad412d927",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R004","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g08-e12"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-8571e493b8ecf84a","target":"COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","source_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","target_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","target_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Day-ahead implementation assumption in the reported simulation case sets; retained under the evidence's SDR mechanism registration. | Reported simulation convergence stopping criterion. | SDR implementation model. | Standard current-price decision-making in the P2P simulation framework, illustrated by the Appendix B SDR example. | The SDR exit mechanism attributed to Ref. [17]. | The proposed last-defence mechanism used in this paper's P2P simulation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g04-EV07","v141-b-g04-EV08","v141-b-g07-ev-11","v141-b-g08-e12"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"e757972a7890e5ca284f7f87f3585a77ac73b49d3e1e812f12005dddd613b490","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Internal prices are tariff-bounded functions of the zone supply-demand ratio, with distinct buying/selling roles for net power signs. For SDR above one both equal the export tariff; for SDR between zero and one retain the source nonlinear selling-price formula and buying-price cost/balance construction. Do not generalize denominator limits or fee accounting beyond source conditions.","target_definition":"The current internal market price guides each participant's decentralized decision to maximize its individual economic benefit. Scope: Standard current-price decision-making in the P2P simulation framework, illustrated by the Appendix B SDR example. Condition: Participants use the current iteration's internal price, without the optional learning-process modification. The SDR mechanism adopts an iterative bidding and pricing process for price-signal coordination. Scope: SDR implementation model. The bidding and pricing process for price-signal coordination is assumed to be conducted on a day-ahead basis. Scope: Day-ahead implementation assumption in the reported simulation case sets; retained under the evidence's SDR mechanism registration. Condition: The simulations assume accurate generation and demand forecasts for each customer. The iterative price-coordination simulation stops and is treated as converged when the stated price-difference criterion is met. Scope: Reported simulation convergence stopping criterion. Condition: The maximum internal price difference between two consecutive iterations is less than 0.001 £/kWh. The iterative price-coordination simulation terminates at the iteration limit whether or not convergence has been achieved. Scope: The proposed last-defence mechanism used in this paper's P2P simulation. Condition: The predefined finite iteration limit is reached. The iterative price-coordination simulation is forced to exit when it reaches the iteration limit without converging. Scope: The SDR exit mechanism attributed to Ref. [17]. Condition: The maximum number of iterations is reached without convergence.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The current internal market price guides each participant's decentralized decision to maximize its individual economic benefit. Scope: Standard current-price decision-making in the P2P simulation framework, illustrated by the Appendix B SDR example. Condition: Participants use the current iteration's internal price, without the optional learning-process modification.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g08-e12"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e25","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.2","anchor_text":"ternal price at the current iteration), while with a learning process, it is si assumed that the pro","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Another technique is to involve a learning process in the decision-making model of each prosumer agent. Traditionally, as described in Formula (3), the objective of each prosumer agent is to maximise its economic beneﬁts given the current market environment (i.e. the internal price at the current iteration), while with a learning process, it is assumed that the prosumer agents make decisions not only considering the current situation but also referring to the historical experience and/or the forecast for the future. This assumption is basically sensible because the prosumer agents, either human beings or computer programs, can have the intelligence to learn from the past and predict the future when making decisions. If the learning process is designed properly, the convergence of the simulation is able to be enhanced."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g08-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p29-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":29,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Note that the schedule becomes exactly the same as the initial schedule. The iterations, and the sim","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. B3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-29.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Observing the iterative process of the above example (as showcased by Formulae (B2)–(B6) and illustrated in Figs. B1 and B2), it is seen that actually the SDR mechanism gave the right incentive signal every time (i.e. the internal prices motivated Prosumer A to change the schedule to use excess local PV generation from Prosumer B), but due to the discontinuity of the demand function, Prosumer A over-adjusted its power consumption every time, resulting in the oscillation-like divergence. Considering this fact, it is natural to be proposed to limit the change of power consumption of each prosumer for avoiding divergence. Therefore, now assume that at each iteration, Prosumer A is only allowed to at most make a ± 0.1 kW change to its schedule for each time slot. Also assume that Prosumer A will not change its schedule if no more cost can be saved. Keep all the other settings the same, and then run the simulation again. The results are shown in Figs. B3 and B4."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Day-ahead implementation assumption in the reported simulation case sets; retained under the evidence's SDR mechanism registration. | Reported simulation convergence stopping criterion. | SDR implementation model. | Standard current-price decision-making in the P2P simulation framework, illustrated by the Appendix B SDR example. | The SDR exit mechanism attributed to Ref. [17]. | The proposed last-defence mechanism used in this paper's P2P simulation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g04-EV07","v141-b-g04-EV08","v141-b-g07-ev-11","v141-b-g08-e12"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e25","v141-b-g08-e12"]},"paper_scope_note":"SDR, MMR, and BS are kept separate; the A18 net quantity differs from the A24 independent component; optional step-size control and the divergent loop in the example are not treated as general convergence or necessary dependencies."}});
